    "status": "verified-lecture study filter",
    "basis": "High-yield labels are derived from supplied lecture definitions, canonical worked examples, edge cases, and Project 1/homework relevance. They are not past-paper evidence or a guarantee of exam appearance.",
    "highYieldTopics": [
      "Ch1: DBMS purpose and file-system limitations",
      "Ch1: physical/logical/view levels, schema versus instance, and physical data independence",
      "Ch1: DDL versus DML, logical versus physical design, query processor, execution plan, and transactions",
      "Ch2: domains, keys, referential integrity, and the University schema",
      "Ch2: selection, projection, Cartesian product, joins, set compatibility, rename, and query equivalence",
      "Ch2: redundancy, anomalies, and the decomposition bridge",
      "Ch3: DDL and integrity constraints, especially foreign-key behavior",
      "Ch3: SELECT-FROM-WHERE, joins, aliases, duplicates, set operations, NULL, and three-valued logic",
      "Ch3: aggregation, GROUP BY, HAVING, BIG 6, nested queries, quantifiers, EXISTS, and NOT EXISTS",
      "Ch3: CTEs, scalar subqueries, INSERT/DELETE/UPDATE safety, cascades, and MySQL restrictions"
    ],
